{% comment %}
  "WHY YOU'LL LOVE IT" - a small uppercase label, one serif line, and a stack
  of icon + heading + body rows on a sand card, closed by a full-bleed image.

  The copy is per product and comes from metafields; the icons are per template
  and come from block settings. Which metafield a row reads is decided by its
  position, so the first block reads custom.usp_1_heading / custom.usp_1_text,
  the second reads usp_2_*, and so on up to usp_6_*. Reordering the blocks in
  the theme editor reorders which metafield shows where, which is the behaviour
  a merchant dragging a row expects.

  Each row falls back to text typed on its own block when the metafield is
  empty, so the section is visible and editable before any metafield exists.
  Filling the metafield on a product overrides the fallback for that product
  only - which is the point: the fallback is the collection-level claim, the
  metafield is the one true of this specific garment.

  A row with neither is skipped, and the section renders nothing at all when
  no row survives, so clearing all the fallbacks is how you turn it off.

  One row can be marked "Highlight", which inverts it to the brand green and
  bleeds it to the card's edges - the design uses it for "Made in small
  batches", which used to be a full-width band of its own. Marking two rows
  works, but the design intends one.

  Every part of the card can come from the product, not just the copy. The
  block settings stay exactly as they were and every one of them still works -
  they are the fallback, and the theme editor is unchanged. What the metafields
  add is the ability to say something different on one product without adding a
  template for it.

  Metafields read:
  - custom.usp_label                              (single line text)
  - custom.usp_lede                               (single line text)
  - custom.usp_media                              (file: image or video)
  - custom.usp_1_heading .. custom.usp_6_heading  (single line text)
  - custom.usp_1_text    .. custom.usp_6_text     (multi-line text)
  - custom.usp_1_icon    .. custom.usp_6_icon     (single line text, icon name)
  - custom.usp_1_highlight .. usp_6_highlight     (true/false)

  Two consequences worth knowing about:

  - The rows are the six numbered slots, not the blocks. A product can fill
    usp_6_heading on a template that only has five blocks and the sixth row
    appears, with the icon from usp_6_icon. That is the point of numbering them
    - a row is a position, and a block is only the default copy for it.

  - custom.usp_media takes one file and works out what it is. An image renders
    as the photo, a video renders as a real <video> with the section's autoplay,
    loop, mute and controls settings applied to it. So the merchant uploads
    whatever the shoot produced without choosing a field first, and the section
    behaves the same either way. A YouTube or Vimeo link is still a section
    setting, because Shopify has no metafield type that holds one as an
    embeddable video rather than as a bare string.
{% endcomment %}

{{ 'product-page.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- liquid
  comment
    The section label and the opening line, per product where the product says
    so. Resolved the same way as everything else here: the metafield if it has
    one, the block or section setting if it does not.
  endcomment
  assign section_label = product.metafields.custom.usp_label.value | default: product.metafields.custom.usp_label
  if section_label == blank
    assign section_label = section.settings.heading
  endif

  assign section_lede = product.metafields.custom.usp_lede.value | default: product.metafields.custom.usp_lede
  if section_lede == blank
    assign section_lede = section.settings.lede
  endif

  assign rendered = 0
  assign headings = ''
  assign bodies = ''
  assign icons = ''
  assign highlights = ''

  comment
    Six slots, walked by number, rather than a loop over the blocks.

    The mapping is the same one the blocks always had - slot 1 is the first
    block, slot 2 the second - so dragging a row in the theme editor still
    reorders which metafield shows where, and nothing about an existing
    template changes. What it also allows is a slot with a metafield and no
    block behind it: a product that fills usp_6_heading on a five-block
    template gets a sixth row rather than silently losing it. Six because that
    is the block limit and the documented range of the keys.
  endcomment
  for i in (1..6)
    assign row_block = section.blocks[forloop.index0]

    assign heading_key = 'usp_' | append: i | append: '_heading'
    assign text_key = 'usp_' | append: i | append: '_text'
    assign icon_key = 'usp_' | append: i | append: '_icon'
    assign highlight_key = 'usp_' | append: i | append: '_highlight'

    assign heading = product.metafields.custom[heading_key].value | default: product.metafields.custom[heading_key]
    assign body = product.metafields.custom[text_key].value | default: product.metafields.custom[text_key]
    assign icon = product.metafields.custom[icon_key].value | default: product.metafields.custom[icon_key]

    comment
      Fall back per field rather than per row: a product that has a heading
      metafield but no body should keep the block's body, not lose it.
    endcomment
    if heading == blank
      assign heading = row_block.settings.heading
    endif
    if body == blank
      assign body = row_block.settings.text
    endif
    if icon == blank
      assign icon = row_block.settings.icon
    endif
    comment
      'none' rather than nothing when no icon resolves - which is what happens
      on a slot with no block behind it. An empty string appended to the list
      below would leave two delimiters together and shift every icon after it
      onto the wrong row. 'none' is already the value the render loop reads as
      "draw no icon", so the sentinel and the setting are the same thing.
    endcomment
    if icon == blank
      assign icon = 'none'
    endif

    comment
      Highlight is a boolean, so "the product has not decided" cannot be told
      from "the product says no" by looking at the value - false and nil both
      read as blank. The type is only readable when the metafield exists, so
      that is what decides whether the product has an opinion at all.
    endcomment
    assign highlight_field = product.metafields.custom[highlight_key]
    if highlight_field.type == 'boolean'
      assign highlight = highlight_field.value
    else
      assign highlight = row_block.settings.highlight
    endif

    if heading != blank
      assign rendered = rendered | plus: 1
      assign headings = headings | append: heading | append: '~|~'
      comment
        A blank body is the one entry allowed to be empty. `split` keeps an
        empty entry between two delimiters, so an interior blank still holds
        its position; a blank on the last row is dropped instead, and a body
        list one short is read as nil at that index - which renders no body,
        which is exactly what a blank body means. Nothing else here can be
        empty, because a shifted icon or flag would attach to the wrong row.
      endcomment
      assign bodies = bodies | append: body | append: '~|~'
      assign icons = icons | append: icon | append: '~|~'
      comment
        Flags carry a value for every surviving row so this list stays the same
        length as the other three and can be read by the same index. A bare
        boolean appended to a string is '' when false, which would collapse two
        entries into one.
      endcomment
      if highlight
        assign highlights = highlights | append: '1' | append: '~|~'
      else
        assign highlights = highlights | append: '0' | append: '~|~'
      endif
    endif
  endfor

  assign heading_list = headings | split: '~|~'
  assign body_list = bodies | split: '~|~'
  assign icon_list = icons | split: '~|~'
  assign highlight_list = highlights | split: '~|~'
-%}

{%- if rendered > 0 -%}
  <div
    class="pdp-section pdp-why color-{{ section.settings.color_scheme }} gradient"
    style="--pdp-pad-top: {{ section.settings.padding_top }}px; --pdp-pad-bottom: {{ section.settings.padding_bottom }}px;"
  >
    <div class="pdp-section__inner">
      {%- comment -%}
        `--split` rather than `:has(.pdp-why__media)`, so the two-column rule
        keys off something Liquid knows for certain. Without an image there is
        no second column to fill, and a card that went to two columns anyway
        would put half a page of empty sand beside the rows.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- liquid
        comment
          One answer for the class, the ratio and the render, rather than
          several conditions that can disagree.

          The product's own file wins over everything on the section, because
          that is the whole point of it; within the section a Shopify-hosted
          video wins over an external URL, and either wins over the image. So a
          merchant who uploads a video to a product that already had a section
          photo gets the video, and clearing the metafield puts the photo back.

          `custom.usp_media` is one file field holding either an image or a
          video, and which it is has to be sniffed rather than asked: an image
          file reference returns a drop with no media_type at all, so the test
          is for a property only one of them has - `sources` for a video,
          `width` for an image. A list metafield is accepted too and its first
          entry used, so a merchant who defined the field as a list rather than
          a single file is not left with a card that renders nothing.
        endcomment
        assign mf_media = product.metafields.custom.usp_media
        assign mf_file = mf_media.value
        if mf_media.type contains 'list.'
          assign mf_file = mf_media.value.first
        endif

        assign media_kind = ''
        if mf_file.sources.size > 0 or mf_file.media_type == 'video'
          assign media_kind = 'product_video'
        elsif mf_file.width > 0
          assign media_kind = 'product_image'
        elsif section.settings.video != blank
          assign media_kind = 'video'
        elsif section.settings.video_url != blank
          assign media_kind = 'embed'
        elsif section.settings.image != blank
          assign media_kind = 'image'
        endif

        assign has_video = false
        if media_kind == 'product_video' or media_kind == 'video' or media_kind == 'embed'
          assign has_video = true
        endif

        assign has_media = false
        if media_kind != blank
          assign has_media = true
        endif

        comment
          Muting is forced on wherever autoplay is on, for every video source.
          Every browser blocks an unmuted autoplay and the failure is silent - a
          poster frame that never moves and nothing in the console.
        endcomment
        assign v_muted = section.settings.video_mute
        if section.settings.video_autoplay
          assign v_muted = true
        endif

        assign split = '1fr 1fr'
        if section.settings.desktop_split == 'copy'
          assign split = '1.25fr 0.75fr'
        elsif section.settings.desktop_split == 'media'
          assign split = '0.75fr 1.25fr'
        endif
      -%}
      <div
        class="pdp-why__card{% if has_media %} pdp-why__card--split{% endif %}{% if section.settings.mobile_media_first %} pdp-why__card--media-first{% endif %}"
        style="--pdp-why-split: {{ split }};{% if section.settings.media_ratio != 'adapt' %} --pdp-why-ratio: {{ section.settings.media_ratio }};{% endif %}"
      >
        <div class="pdp-why__content">
          {%- if section_label != blank -%}
            <p class="pdp-eyebrow pdp-why__label">{{ section_label | escape }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if section_lede != blank -%}
            <p class="pdp-why__lede">{{ section_lede | escape }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}

          <ul class="pdp-why__list">
            {%- for heading in heading_list -%}
              {%- assign is_highlight = false -%}
              {%- if highlight_list[forloop.index0] == '1' -%}
                {%- assign is_highlight = true -%}
              {%- endif -%}
              <li class="pdp-why__row{% if is_highlight %} pdp-why__row--highlight{% endif %}">
                {%- assign icon_name = icon_list[forloop.index0] -%}
                {%- if icon_name != blank and icon_name != 'none' -%}
                  <span class="pdp-why__icon">
                    {%- render 'pdp-icon', icon: icon_name -%}
                  </span>
                {%- endif -%}
                <div class="pdp-why__body">
                  <h3 class="pdp-why__heading">{{ heading | escape }}</h3>
                  {%- assign body = body_list[forloop.index0] -%}
                  {%- if body != blank -%}
                    <p class="pdp-why__text">{{ body | escape | newline_to_br }}</p>
                  {%- endif -%}
                </div>
              </li>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </ul>
        </div>

        {%- comment -%}
          The media. Outside .pdp-why__content, so it reaches the card's edges
          without cancelling the content's padding: from 990px it is the card's
          second column, below that it stacks - above the rows by default,
          because that is where the reviewed mobile design puts it.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if has_media -%}
          <div class="pdp-why__media{% if has_video %} pdp-why__media--video{% endif %}{% if section.settings.media_ratio != 'adapt' %} pdp-why__media--ratio{% endif %}">
            {%- if media_kind == 'product_video' -%}
              {%- comment -%}
                The product's own video file. Rendered with exactly the section's
                autoplay, loop, mute and controls settings, so a merchant who
                swaps the section video for a per-product one does not also have
                to re-set how it plays - which is the "settings stay the same"
                half of this section being product-driven.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {{
                mf_file
                | video_tag:
                  image_size: '1400x',
                  autoplay: section.settings.video_autoplay,
                  loop: section.settings.video_loop,
                  muted: v_muted,
                  controls: section.settings.video_controls,
                  preload: 'metadata'
              }}
            {%- elsif media_kind == 'product_image' -%}
              {{
                mf_file
                | image_url: width: 1400
                | image_tag:
                  loading: 'lazy',
                  sizes: '(min-width: 990px) 50vw, 100vw',
                  widths: '400, 600, 800, 1000, 1200, 1400',
                  alt: mf_file.alt
              }}
            {%- elsif media_kind == 'video' -%}
              {%- comment -%}
                A Shopify-hosted video, so autoplay, muting and looping are
                attributes on a real <video> rather than provider query
                parameters.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {{
                section.settings.video
                | video_tag:
                  image_size: '1400x',
                  autoplay: section.settings.video_autoplay,
                  loop: section.settings.video_loop,
                  muted: v_muted,
                  controls: section.settings.video_controls,
                  preload: 'metadata'
              }}
            {%- elsif media_kind == 'embed' -%}
              {%- comment -%}
                YouTube and Vimeo do not take the same parameters: YouTube wants
                `mute` and needs `playlist` set to its own id before `loop` does
                anything at all, Vimeo wants `muted`. Sending one provider the
                other's names is accepted and ignored, which looks like the
                setting simply not working.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              <div class="pdp-why__embed">
                {%- if section.settings.video_url.type == 'youtube' -%}
                  {{
                    section.settings.video_url
                    | external_video_url:
                      autoplay: section.settings.video_autoplay,
                      mute: section.settings.video_autoplay,
                      loop: section.settings.video_loop,
                      playlist: section.settings.video_url.id,
                      controls: section.settings.video_controls
                    | external_video_tag: loading: 'lazy'
                  }}
                {%- else -%}
                  {{
                    section.settings.video_url
                    | external_video_url:
                      autoplay: section.settings.video_autoplay,
                      muted: section.settings.video_autoplay,
                      loop: section.settings.video_loop,
                      controls: section.settings.video_controls
                    | external_video_tag: loading: 'lazy'
                  }}
                {%- endif -%}
              </div>
            {%- else -%}
              {{
                section.settings.image
                | image_url: width: 1400
                | image_tag:
                  loading: 'lazy',
                  sizes: '(min-width: 990px) 50vw, 100vw',
                  widths: '400, 600, 800, 1000, 1200, 1400',
                  alt: section.settings.image.alt
              }}
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "PDP: Why you'll love it",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "pdp-section-wrapper",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Everything here is a fallback. A product that fills the matching metafield shows its own instead, and a product that does not shows what is typed here — so this section can be set up once and then said differently on any product without a new template."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Row one reads custom.usp_1_heading, usp_1_text, usp_1_icon and usp_1_highlight; row two reads usp_2_*, and so on to usp_6_*. A row with no heading from either source is hidden, and a product can fill a row this section has no block for."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Icon names for usp_N_icon: leaf, flower, needle, shield, box, feather, hand, weave, block-print, garment, tag, exchange, process, person, truck, clock, check, calendar, or none. Anything else draws no icon."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The label and opening line below read custom.usp_label and custom.usp_lede."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Section label",
      "default": "Why you'll love it",
      "info": "The small uppercase line above the card."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "lede",
      "label": "Opening line",
      "default": "Clothes with character, made for comfort.",
      "info": "One serif line under the label. Leave empty to hide it."
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "image",
      "label": "Closing image",
      "info": "Sits at the foot of the card, full width. Leave empty to hide it."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Media"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "custom.usp_media on the product wins over everything here. It is one file field that takes either an image or a video and works out which — the video plays with the settings below, so nothing needs re-setting per product."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Otherwise: a video wins over the image, and an uploaded video wins over a link. Clear the video to go back to the photo."
    },
    {
      "type": "video",
      "id": "video",
      "label": "Video (uploaded)"
    },
    {
      "type": "video_url",
      "id": "video_url",
      "label": "Video link",
      "accept": [
        "youtube",
        "vimeo"
      ],
      "info": "Used only when no uploaded video is set."
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "video_autoplay",
      "label": "Autoplay",
      "default": true,
      "info": "Muting is forced on while autoplay is on — browsers block an unmuted autoplay silently."
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "video_mute",
      "label": "Mute",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "video_loop",
      "label": "Loop",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "video_controls",
      "label": "Show player controls",
      "default": false
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "media_ratio",
      "label": "Media shape",
      "default": "adapt",
      "info": "Applies where the media stacks under 990px. From 990px it is one half of the card and fills that column's height.",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "adapt",
          "label": "Adapt to the media"
        },
        {
          "value": "1 / 1",
          "label": "Square (1:1)"
        },
        {
          "value": "4 / 5",
          "label": "Portrait (4:5)"
        },
        {
          "value": "3 / 4",
          "label": "Portrait (3:4)"
        },
        {
          "value": "4 / 3",
          "label": "Landscape (4:3)"
        },
        {
          "value": "3 / 2",
          "label": "Landscape (3:2)"
        },
        {
          "value": "16 / 9",
          "label": "Wide (16:9)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "desktop_split",
      "label": "Desktop split",
      "default": "even",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "even",
          "label": "Even halves"
        },
        {
          "value": "copy",
          "label": "Wider copy"
        },
        {
          "value": "media",
          "label": "Wider media"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "mobile_media_first",
      "label": "Show media first on mobile",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "color_scheme",
      "id": "color_scheme",
      "label": "t:sections.all.colors.label",
      "default": "scheme-1"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:sections.all.padding.section_padding_heading"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_top",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "t:sections.all.padding.padding_top",
      "default": 48
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_bottom",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "t:sections.all.padding.padding_bottom",
      "default": 48
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "column",
      "name": "Row",
      "limit": 6,
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "select",
          "id": "icon",
          "label": "Icon",
          "info": "Used when this row's usp_N_icon metafield is empty.",
          "default": "leaf",
          "options": [
            {
              "value": "none",
              "label": "None"
            },
            {
              "value": "leaf",
              "label": "Leaf"
            },
            {
              "value": "flower",
              "label": "Flower"
            },
            {
              "value": "needle",
              "label": "Needle and thread"
            },
            {
              "value": "shield",
              "label": "Shield"
            },
            {
              "value": "box",
              "label": "Parcel"
            },
            {
              "value": "feather",
              "label": "Feather"
            },
            {
              "value": "hand",
              "label": "Hand"
            },
            {
              "value": "weave",
              "label": "Weave"
            },
            {
              "value": "block-print",
              "label": "Block print"
            },
            {
              "value": "garment",
              "label": "Garment"
            },
            {
              "value": "tag",
              "label": "Tag"
            },
            {
              "value": "exchange",
              "label": "Exchange"
            },
            {
              "value": "process",
              "label": "Process"
            },
            {
              "value": "person",
              "label": "Person"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "heading",
          "label": "Heading",
          "info": "Used when this row's metafield is empty."
        },
        {
          "type": "textarea",
          "id": "text",
          "label": "Text",
          "info": "Used when this row's metafield is empty."
        },
        {
          "type": "checkbox",
          "id": "highlight",
          "label": "Highlight this row",
          "default": false,
          "info": "Inverts the row to the brand green and bleeds it to the card's edges. The design uses this on one row only. A product's usp_N_highlight metafield overrides it either way."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "PDP: Why you'll love it",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "leaf"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "flower"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "needle"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "shield"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "box",
            "highlight": true
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
